# Priority 4 prep — second backend MVP (not implemented)

**Status:** scaffold only. Backend-C remains the only working floor.  
**See:** `FLOOR.oot` F3, `RUNTIME_ABI_v0.oot`.

---

## Goal of F3 (when scheduled)

Prove the language is **not C-monoculture** by running **one** CHS smoke on a non-C floor — **without** deleting Backend-C or requiring full oodac self-host on the new floor.

### MVP definition of done

| Check | Criterion |
|-------|-----------|
| Emit | New package (e.g. `emit_wasm_*.oo` or seed-ABI) produces artifact for `fixtures/chs_list_string.oo` or `while_count.oo` |
| Run | Artifact executes and prints expected smoke output |
| Flag | `oodac build --backend <x>` works for that backend; `--backend c` still green |
| Rails | Backend-C fixed_point + smokes **still green** |
| Docs | ABI mapping table: CHS smoke **called** symbols → new floor |

### Out of scope for MVP

- Full oodac multi-module self-host on new backend  
- Deleting `runtime/chs_rt*.c`  
- Beta claim  

---

## Candidate backends (pick one later)

| ID | Approach | Floor trade | Fit for CHS smoke |
|----|----------|-------------|-------------------|
| **W** | Emit WASM text/binary + run with wasmtime/wasm3 | Needs WASM runtime | Good demos |
| **L** | Emit LLVM IR + clang/llc | LLVM/C++ toolchain | Strong native |
| **S** | Seed ABI: emit only calls into seed-provided ops | Fatter seed, no gcc for app | Max “no C source tree” for apps |

**Recommendation when starting F3:** **W** or **S** first (clearer escape from gcc-as-app-link than L).

---

## File layout (proposed — do not create until F3 starts)

```text
oodac/
  emit_c_*.oo          # rename optional; today c_emit_*.oo
  emit_<backend>_*.oo  # new
scripts/
  link_<backend>.sh    # link/load recipe
bootstrap/
  RUNTIME_ABI_v0.oot    # map subset to backend
```

---

## Flag reservation (done in F2)

- `oodac [--backend c] <cmd> …` — only `c` accepted; else `ERR backend … residual`  
- `ooda build --backend c` — same  

When F3 lands: accept second name without breaking `c`.

---

## Residual honesty

Until F3 ships, **any** non-`c` backend string is fail-closed residual.  
Host residual symbols (`oo_host_*`, `oo_chs_build`) are **not** declared in pure Backend-C
preamble (removed); optional only under `OODA_WITH_HOST_FFI` in `chs_rt_host.c` — see ABI v0.

